/**
 * @defgroup MCC_Workflows_Migration Legacy Migration Backlog
 * @ingroup MCC_Workflows
 * @brief Controlled reconstruction plan for the historical MCC codebases.
 *
 * Historical code is design input, not source to copy without review. Every
 * migrated concept must define its namespace, ownership, invalid states,
 * embedded constraints, Foundation dependencies, tests, examples, and Doxygen
 * contract before becoming public.
 *
 * | ID | State | Candidate domain |
 * | -- | ----- | ---------------- |
 * | MIG-001 | `NEXT` | Inventory and reconcile legacy public concepts |
 * | MIG-002 | `TODO` | Pitch: letters, accidentals, octave, ordering |
 * | MIG-003 | `TODO` | Musical note and textual formatting |
 * | MIG-004 | `TODO` | Musical interval representation and arithmetic |
 * | MIG-005 | `TODO` | Scale structure, properties, and definitions |
 * | MIG-006 | `TODO` | MIDI note, message, and protocol representations |
 * | MIG-007 | `TODO` | Evaluate communications/ports as a separate library |
 * | MIG-008 | `TODO` | Validate MCC as a dependency of MIDILAR |
 *
 * Communications, hardware ports, and runtime MIDI transports should not enter
 * the composition core merely because they existed in an old monolithic tree.
 * Their ownership will be decided during the inventory.
 */
